  [38;5;153mtruncate('abcdefg', 5)[39m → [38;5;153m'ab...'[39m. [38;5;153mn[39m caps the total as you chose. Agent-decided edge cases: [38;5;153mn < 4[39m → bare cut with no
  marker (the marker can't fit the cap); negative [38;5;153mn[39m → [38;5;153m''[39m; non-integer [38;5;153mn[39m → floored; missing/non-numeric [38;5;153mn[39m → unchanged.

  [1mTwo things worth your call[0m

  - [1mBoth helpers coerce non-strings via [38;5;153mString()[0m, so [38;5;153mslugify(null)[39m returns the slug [38;5;153m'null'[39m rather than [38;5;153m''[39m. Defensible,
    but it silently turns a bug upstream into plausible-looking output. Throwing, or mapping nullish to [38;5;153m''[39m, may suit you
    better.
  - [1m[38;5;153msrc/slugify.js:5[39m uses a literal combining-mark range[0m — the regex contains raw invisible U+0300–U+036F characters
    rather than [38;5;153m\u0300-\u036f[39m. It passes, but invisible characters in source survive editors and copy-paste poorly.
    One-line fix if you want it.

